NUM-08: book only the excess over full volume as overflow when a node first floods

getFloodedDepth() set a non-ponding node's overflow to the whole net inflow
of the step (dV/dt) and its volume to fullVolume. On the step the node first
floods it started below full, so the volume that filled it was counted as
storage and again as overflow. Set the overflow to what is left after the
node fills: (oldVolume + dV - fullVolume)/dt, not below zero. Steps that start
full, and plain junctions (fullVolume = 0), are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-08_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c b/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c
index 972da8c..1f1feec 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c
@@ -814,7 +814,9 @@ double getFloodedDepth(int i, int canPond, double dV, double yNew,
 {
     if ( canPond == FALSE )
     {
-        Node[i].overflow = dV / dt;
+        // --- overflow is what is left after the node fills to fullVolume
+        Node[i].overflow = MAX(0.0, Node[i].oldVolume + dV -
+                                    Node[i].fullVolume) / dt;
         Node[i].newVolume = Node[i].fullVolume;
         yNew = yMax;
     }
